    <!-- Main Content Overlapping Hero -->
    <main class="flex-1 max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full px-6 py-8 -mt-16 relative z-20 macos-glass mb-12">
        
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4"><span class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/10 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-1"><svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg> 2 MIN READ</span></div><div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-white/10 pb-6">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">Scripture Memory</h2>
            <div class="w-24 h-1 rounded-full opacity-80" style="background-color: #6366f1"></div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="prose  max-w-none">
            <div class="mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>Why Memorize Scripture?</h3>
                <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Psalm 119:11 says it plainly: "I have hidden your word in my heart, that I might not sin against you." Scripture memory isn't an optional spiritual hobby — it's warfare. The enemy speaks in lies, and the only weapon that silences him is the living Word of God planted deep inside you. When Jesus was tempted in the wilderness, He didn't argue with the devil, He didn't try to reason His way out — He responded three times with "It is written" (Matthew 4:1-11).</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">If the Son of God fought temptation with memorized Scripture, what makes us think we can survive without it? You fight lies with truth, and truth has to live in you before it can defend you. In a world that bombards you with false narratives about your identity, your worth, and your future, the Word of God hidden in your heart becomes your anchor and your sword.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>The Practical Power</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">When anxiety hits at 2 AM and your chest is tight and your mind is racing, you won't have time to grab your phone and search for a Bible verse — you need truth already loaded in your spirit. When temptation comes knocking and the pull feels overwhelming, you need a word from God that rises up from within you before your flesh can respond. When a friend is sitting across from you in tears, broken and searching for hope, you become a living carrier of God's Word — not just someone who knows where to find it, but someone who can speak it from the heart.</p><div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Joshua 1:8 tells us to meditate on the Word day and night so that we may be careful to do everything written in it — and then we will be prosperous and successful. This isn't prosperity gospel; this is the promise that a Word-saturated life produces a Spirit-led life. Scripture memory turns passive believers into people who are ready in season and out of season.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>Our Memory System</h3>
                <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">We use a simple, proven card-based system designed for real life — not seminary students, but busy young adults with jobs, classes, and full schedules. The rhythm is straightforward: one verse per week, reviewed daily, and carried with you wherever you go. Write it on an index card, set it as your lock screen, stick it on your mirror — whatever it takes to keep the Word in front of your eyes.</p><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">By the end of the year, you'll have 52 verses hidden in your heart, and that's a spiritual arsenal that will change how you think, how you pray, and how you fight. But here's the part that makes it stick: we do it together as a community. You'll have an accountability partner who texts you, a small group that recites together, and a culture that celebrates the Word.</p><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">You weren't meant to do this alone, and in this ministry, you won't.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>Getting Started</h3>
                <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Don't overthink it — just start. Begin with these foundational verses that every believer should carry in their heart: John 3:16 (the gospel in one sentence), Romans 8:28 (God's sovereignty over your pain), Philippians 4:6-7 (the antidote to anxiety), Proverbs 3:5-6 (trusting God over your own understanding), and Isaiah 41:10 (courage when fear is loud). Pick one — just one — and write it down.</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">Say it out loud in the morning before you check your phone. Repeat it at night before you close your eyes. Carry it with you through the day and watch how the Holy Spirit brings it to mind exactly when you need it.</p><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">This is how transformation begins — not in dramatic moments, but in daily, faithful repetition. The Word works. Trust the process, and watch what God does in you and through you.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-white/10">
